WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:06.076
Hi, I am Professor Vector. Today: what does equal groups mean?

2
00:00:06.136 --> 00:00:11.824
Here are three crates for bolts.

3
00:00:11.884 --> 00:00:22.410
Each crate gets four bolts. Every group is the same size, so these are equal groups.

4
00:00:22.470 --> 00:00:28.574
Count them all: four, eight, twelve. That is three groups of four.

5
00:00:28.634 --> 00:00:35.168
We write it as three times four equals twelve. Times means groups of.

6
00:00:35.228 --> 00:00:42.620
Line the groups up in rows and you get an array: three rows of four.

7
00:00:42.680 --> 00:00:53.944
Turn the array on its side: four rows of three. Still twelve bolts. So three times four is the same as four times three.

8
00:00:54.004 --> 00:01:03.517
If the groups are not equal, it is not multiplication. Two, five and three have to be added: ten.

9
00:01:03.577 --> 00:01:10.880
Your turn. Five crates with two bolts in each. How many bolts?

10
00:01:10.940 --> 00:01:18.333
Ten! Five groups of two: two, four, six, eight, ten. Five times two equals ten.

11
00:01:18.393 --> 00:01:24.553
Now try it yourself. The worked example is waiting in your lesson.
